  "gameDescriptionHtml": "\n<b><i>“Good luck, have fun, and expect nothing good.”</i></b><p></p>\n<p><b>ABSOLUTELY NOTHING GOOD</b> is a first-person game created for Halloween, combining everyday work at a roadside store, supernatural events, elements of psychological horror, and dark humor.</p>\n<p>Halloween is approaching — the one night of the year when the boundary between the worlds of the living and the dead grows thinner.</p>\n<p>The night before Halloween was supposed to be business as usual: holiday preparations, routine chores, and the occasional late-night customer. But this time, the silence outside the store is disturbed by the presence of someone who should still be locked away.</p>\n<p><b>Game Features:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>An atmospheric first-person game with elements of psychological horror and shop simulation\n</li><li>Night shifts filled with everyday tasks and unusual customers\n</li><li>A gradually unfolding supernatural story with no combat\n</li><li>Comic-inspired visuals with adjustable pixelation\n</li><li>Atmospheric sound design\n</li><li>Average playtime: approximately 60 minutes\n</li><li>The 2D mini-game is available under “Select Level” in the main menu\n</li></ul>\n",
